---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
	<div class="page-shell prose">
		<section aria-labelledby="about-heading">
			<p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
			<h1 id="about-heading">Tracing the Kirkbride Plan.</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				Asylum Atlas is an independent, sourced directory of former and surviving U.S. sites
				associated with the Kirkbride Plan.
			</p>
			<p>
				Use the map to explore sites by name, location, current status, and available imagery. Each
				record keeps its history, uncertainty, and sources visible.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="methodology-heading">
			<p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
			<h2 id="methodology-heading">A map built from records, not lore.</h2>
			<p class="lead">
				Asylum Atlas documents verified former and surviving U.S. institutions and buildings
				explicitly identified by reputable sources as following the Kirkbride Plan.
			</p><h2>What belongs here</h2><p>
				We map the physical campus or building. A single institution can therefore appear more than
				once when it occupied distinct qualifying locations. Completed U.S. sites are eligible,
				including demolished sites when their historic location can be established.
			</p><p>
				We exclude unbuilt proposals, non-Kirkbride psychiatric hospitals, later cottage-plan
				campuses, and candidates supported only by unsourced lists. Questionable candidates belong
				in the research ledger, not on the public map.
			</p><h2>How records are structured</h2><p>
				Each site has a stable identifier, aliases, dates, architect information, current status,
				location precision, a short original note, and source references. Claim-level references in
				the JSON data make it possible to audit the core fields. Unknown values are left unknown
				rather than guessed.
			</p><h2>Coordinates and access</h2><p>
				Coordinates describe a building or historic campus and are marked exact, campus, or
				approximate. They should not be interpreted as an entrance, an open property, or an
				invitation to visit. Operating healthcare sites may have strict access controls.
			</p><h2>Images and rights</h2><p>
				Images are optional. When added, they must be hosted locally and carry Public Domain, CC0,
				CC BY, or CC BY-SA metadata, source URLs, license links, and visible attribution. This
				prototype has text-only records until compliant image files are verified.
			</p><h2>Independence</h2><p>
				The seed sites at KirkbrideBuildings.com, RootsWeb’s Asylum Projects, and Wikipedia’s
				Kirkbride Plan article are discovery aids and cross-checks. They are not copied sources for
				the site’s prose. Records are independently structured and summaries are original. The
				project is not affiliated with any listed institution or source.
			</p><p><a class="button" href="/">Explore the map ↗</a></p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
	.lead {
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
	.prose .button {
		color: var(--paper);
	}
</style>
